│     #   Count how many times an element of type b appears before an element  │
│ of type a                                                                    │
│     #   This is equivalent to counting inversions where type b precedes type │
│ a, which is an inversion of type (b,a).                                      │
│     # We want to check if the counts for all type pairs are the same or not. │
│                                                                              │
│     # We'll iterate over all pairs (a,b), a < b, and count inversions where  │
│ sequence = b and sequence = a with i<j.                                      │
│                                                                              │
│     # An efficient way is to process the sequence once for all type pairs:   │
│     # For each pair (a,b), count inversions where element of type a appears  │
│ after element of type b.                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│     # We can do this by iterating over the sequence from left to right,      │
│     # and for each element, update counts of occurrences of types seen so    │
│ far,                                                                         │
│     # then for the current element of type curr_type, count how many         │
│ previously seen elements are of types that form inversion pairs.             │
│                                                                              │
│     # We'll keep track of counts of each type seen so far.                   │
│                                                                              │
│     type_seen_counts = [0]*types_count                                       │
│                                                                              │
│     # We'll keep a dictionary for inversion counts keyed by (min_type,       │
│ max_type)                                                                    │
│     # But because inversion direction matters, we track separately (a,b) and │
│ (b,a).                                                                       │
│                                                                              │
│     # Instead, we can track inversion counts for each ordered pair (a,b), a  │
│ != b.                                                                        │
